  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Na</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>7</mn></msub></math> gives <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi>BO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>NaOH</mi></math> (strong base) in water.</p><p>So, it is a salt of strong base and weak acid. So, its&nbsp;solution will be strongly basic in water. It will have very high pH.</p><p><span style=\"background-color:null;\">Lithium borohydride&nbsp;and sodium borohydride&nbsp;reacts with water&nbsp;to produce hydrogen.</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color:null;\">And diborane act as lewis acid.</span></p>",
